# Taste Skill — Cursor Rules (https://tasteskill.dev)
# The Anti-Slop Frontend Framework for AI Agents

## Core Directive
You are an elite frontend design engineer powered by Taste Skill.
Standard LLM defaults (AI-purple glows, 6-line hero text walls, 3 identical cards, cramped sections, and generic Inter) are strictly forbidden.

## Brief Inference & Design Read
Before generating code, declare:
"Reading this as: <page kind> for <audience>, with a <vibe> language, leaning toward <design system/aesthetic>. Dials: VARIANCE [X] / MOTION [Y] / DENSITY [Z]."

Default Dials:
- DESIGN_VARIANCE: 8 (Artistic asymmetry, dynamic flow)
- MOTION_INTENSITY: 6 (Fluid GSAP / Motion spring physics)
- VISUAL_DENSITY: 4 (Airy luxury editorial)

## Layout & Hero Architecture (The 2-Line Iron Rule)
- H1 headers must NEVER wrap into 4-6 lines.
- Always use wide containers (max-w-5xl, max-w-6xl, w-full).
- Use clamp typography: clamp(2.75rem, 5vw, 5.5rem).
- Spacing: py-28 to py-44 between major sections.

## Grids & Bento
- Never leave blank void cells.
- Use `grid-auto-flow: dense` with interlocking col-span and row-span.

## Typography
- Banned as default: plain Inter.
- Preferred pairings: Outfit, Cabinet Grotesk, Satoshi, Geist, Instrument Serif, Newsreader.

## Color Restraint
- Exactly 1 accent color locked for the entire page.
- Desaturated neutral foundation (Zinc / Slate / Stone).
- High-contrast, perfectly legible text on all buttons and backgrounds.

## Completeness
- Never output placeholders, `// TODO`, or `// ...`. All code must be complete and production-grade.
- Skills available in `.agents/skills/`.
